  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global (Ethiopia, Liberia, Malawi, Mauritania, Rwanda, Senegal, Somalia, The Gambia, Uganda): Investment Support Programme (ISP) for the Least-Developed Countries (LDCs)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Governments, state-owned enterprises, and eligible private sector entities in beneficiary Least-Developed Countries.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme aimed to contribute to improve Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) management in beneficiary countries, and level the playing field between Least-Developed Countries (LDCs) and foreign investors on investment-related matters.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide demand-driven legal and technical assistance and complementary capacity development on investment-related matters, including negotiations and dispute settlement, to eligible stakeholders (government, public and private enterprises) in the Least-Developed Countries.</narrative>
  </description>
